  <div class="section-label">West Haven City Actions</div>
  <h2>Local Government Resolutions (2026)</h2>

  <p>West Haven City has authorized several resolutions in 2026 that directly reflect the city's preparation for the SR-177 corridor's arrival. These actions demonstrate that local government is actively planning around the highway's eventual construction — even though no construction timeline exists.</p>

  <ul class="resolution-list">
    <li>
      <strong>Resolution 09-2026</strong>{% cite "whc-res-09-park-plan" %}
      Adoption of Professional Services for Master Park Plan — leveraging planned trail infrastructure from the SR-177 corridor to enhance local recreational connectivity.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resolution 15-2026</strong>{% cite "whc-res-15-3600s" %}
      Construction authorization on 3600 South — road improvements in the project area reflecting anticipated traffic pattern changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resolution 16-2026</strong>{% cite "whc-res-16-5100w-bid" %}
      Award of bid for the 5100 West roadway widening project. West Haven's economic plan also focuses on capturing sales tax revenue from growth stimulated by the highway.{% cite "whc-rob-sant-economic" %}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>April 15, 2026 — City Council Meeting</strong>{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes" %}
      Shawn Warnke (UDOT representative) presented on SR-177 alignment to the West Haven City Council. Meeting agendas and minutes are available through West Haven City's public records pages.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-label">Legal Framework</div>
  <h2>Eminent Domain and Corridor Preservation Law</h2>

  <p>Understanding the distinction between corridor preservation and eminent domain is critical for property owners in the study area.</p>

  <h3>Corridor Preservation (Pre-Funding)</h3>
  <p>Under <strong>Utah Code 72-5-407</strong>,{% cite "utah-72-5-407" %} corridor preservation is explicitly a <em>voluntary</em> process. UDOT cannot use eminent domain to acquire property for corridor preservation on an unfunded project. When UDOT approaches a property owner under this program, the sale is optional.</p>

  <p>Owners who sell to UDOT under the Corridor Preservation Program receive fair market value based on a certified appraisal.{% cite "udot-acquisition-guide" %} UDOT's acquisition services guidance explains valuation, just compensation, offers to purchase, negotiation, relocation assistance, and possible litigation paths for active projects.{% cite "udot-row-acquisition" %} This can be advantageous for owners who wish to sell before final alignment determination.</p>

  <h3>Eminent Domain (Post-Funding)</h3>
  <p>Once the Weber County SR-177 extension enters the <strong>funded construction phase</strong>, UDOT gains eminent domain authority. Properties within the final right-of-way boundary become subject to mandatory acquisition. Affected property owners retain the following rights under Utah law:</p>

  <ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
    <li>Receive a certified appraisal from UDOT</li>
    <li>Commission an independent appraisal at UDOT's expense</li>
    <li>Negotiate the compensation amount</li>
    <li>Seek legal review or challenge compensation through the process available under Utah law</li>
    <li>Receive relocation assistance if vacating the property is required</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <p><strong>Current status:</strong> Because the Weber County extension is unfunded, eminent domain authority does not currently exist. UDOT can only acquire property in this corridor through voluntary transactions under the Corridor Preservation Program. This will change when and if construction funding is allocated.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label">Public Participation Channels</div>
  <h2>How to Follow the State Environmental Study</h2>

  <p>UDOT provides several formal channels for public participation during the State Environmental Study process:</p>

  <ol style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.5;">
    <li><strong>State Environmental Study notification list</strong> — Register at <a href="https://udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension" rel="noopener noreferrer">udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension</a> to receive notification when alignment maps and the Draft State Environmental Study are published.</li>
    <li><strong>Written public comment</strong> — The Draft State Environmental Study comment period (expected Fall 2026) allows written comments that become part of the official project record.</li>
    <li><strong>Public hearing</strong> — UDOT is required to hold a public hearing during the Draft State Environmental Study phase.</li>
    <li><strong>City Council meeting minutes</strong> — West Haven City Council agendas and minutes, including SR-177 presentations, are publicly available at <a href="https://www.westhavenut.gov/government/city_council/agendas_and_minutes.php" rel="noopener noreferrer">westhavenut.gov</a>.</li>
  </ol>

